id: interface/new-yawn-coordinate-resolution-v0.1
title: "Coordinate-complete New Yawn projection"
kind: interface-contract
status: draft-0.1
version: 0.1.0-draft
updated: 2026-09-01

purpose: >
  Let a person begin with one unrestricted signal while the system compiles a
  correctable Yawn coordinate, orientation View, intelligence binding, open
  lacunae, and next inquiry without exposing the ontology as a setup form.
  The projection makes resolution visible without turning completeness,
  intelligence, confidence, activity, or level into human worth or authority.

constitutional_sources:
  orientation: core/orientation.yawn
  questions: question-packets/orientation-nine.yawn
  inquiry_selection: core/inquiry-selection.yawn
  orientation_map: schemas/orientation-map.v0.1.schema.json
  agency_holarchy: schemas/agency-holarchy.v0.2.schema.json
  objective_holon: schemas/objective-holon.v0.1.schema.json
  new_yawn: interface/new-yawn-v0.1.yawn
  projection_and_aperture: core/projection-and-aperture.yawn
  proof_and_boundary: core/proof-and-boundary.yawn

one_model_rule: >
  This contract is a noncanonical View and compiler over the shared YAWN
  ontology. It does not create a parallel orientation packet, personal
  ontology, truth store, Agent identity, authority source, or second holarchy.

surface:
  default_mode: quiet
  top:
    yawn_face:
      fields: [image_or_default_identity_mark, proposed_name, proposed_coordinate, proposed_location_in_holarchy, lifecycle_state]
      rule: >
        Name, coordinate, placement, and identity remain proposed until an
        explicit owner Plant or equivalent canonical event boundary.
    signal_field:
      prompt: "What has your attention?"
      input_rule: "Accept the person's language without requiring ontology terms."
  resolution_grid:
    visual_analogy: "A light contribution-style grid of inspectable square cells."
    default_detail: collapsed
    interaction: >
      Each cell shows only label, state, and whether attention is needed.
      Activation opens its attributed answers, sources, uncertainty, candidate
      updates, and exact ontology coordinates.
    cells:
      - { id: identity, label: "Identity", maps_to: [scope, perspective] }
      - { id: intelligence, label: "Intelligence", maps_to: [provider_bindings, delegated_agents, capabilities] }
      - { id: placement, label: "Place", maps_to: [placement, primary-parent, lateral-relations] }
      - { id: relationship, label: "Relationship", maps_to: [placement, perspective, relationship] }
      - { id: arena, label: "Arena", maps_to: [placement, current-state] }
      - { id: state, label: "State", maps_to: [current-state] }
      - { id: purpose, label: "Purpose", maps_to: [intent, objective-holon] }
      - { id: lacuna, label: "Lacuna", maps_to: [lacuna] }
      - { id: boundary, label: "Boundary", maps_to: [boundary, authority, privacy] }
      - { id: movement, label: "Moves", maps_to: [movement] }
      - { id: proof, label: "Proof", maps_to: [proof] }
      - { id: memory, label: "Memory", maps_to: [sources, events, revisions, replay] }

cell_states:
  allowed: [unknown, proposed, reported, disputed, accepted, stale, blocked, proof_pending, evidenced]
  rules:
    - "Unknown is visible and is not failure."
    - "Proposed content is visually and semantically distinct from accepted content."
    - "A filled cell is not necessarily true, current, authorized, or sufficient."
    - "Cell state derives from attributed records; presentation never mutates canonical state."

intelligence_cell:
  question: "What intelligence is available to this Yawn, and under which relationship?"
  represents: [principal_and_human_participants, replaceable_model_or_provider_bindings, delegated_agents, tools_and_capabilities, accepted_inherited_policies]
  must_show: [identity, role, source_or_provider, capability, authority_scope, freshness_or_connection_state, revocation_path]
  boundaries:
    - "Provider is not Agent identity."
    - "Connection is not capability."
    - "Capability is not permission."
    - "Model confidence is not rightful authority."
    - "Inherited intelligence never silently changes purpose, identity, privacy, or decision rights."

resolution_ladder:
  name: "Yawn resolution"
  range: [0, 10]
  status: noncanonical-derived-view
  rule: >
    Resolution is the highest consecutively satisfied capability band using
    accepted or explicitly attributed evidence. It is not a score of the
    person, consciousness, intelligence, moral worth, certainty, quality, or
    autonomy. Missing information may be appropriate; a lower band may be safer.
  bands:
    - { level: 0, label: "Signal", requires: [source_signal_preserved] }
    - { level: 1, label: "Addressed", requires: [identity_or_subject_proposed, coordinate_proposed] }
    - { level: 2, label: "Situated", requires: [scope, placement_or_named_lacuna] }
    - { level: 3, label: "Related", requires: [principal, perspective, relationship_or_named_lacuna, arena_or_named_lacuna] }
    - { level: 4, label: "Directed", requires: [current_state, intent_or_purpose_status] }
    - { level: 5, label: "Open", requires: [lacunae, disputes_and_alternatives_preserved] }
    - { level: 6, label: "Bounded", requires: [authority, privacy, consent, effect_boundary] }
    - { level: 7, label: "Movable", requires: [candidate_inquiry_hold_or_move, selection_reason] }
    - { level: 8, label: "Testable", requires: [prediction, consequence_target, verifier, falsifier_or_named_absence] }
    - { level: 9, label: "Inheritable", requires: [bounded_working_context, provenance, revision, parent_and_relationship_refs] }
    - { level: 10, label: "Replayable", requires: [authorized_event, consequence, proof_adjudication, sourced_update, replay] }
  anti_gaming:
    - "No level is earned from generated text alone."
    - "A named lacuna may satisfy structural coverage but not evidential closure."
    - "Later levels require the earlier boundaries to remain valid and fresh."
    - "The system must lower or mark a level stale when required evidence expires or is disputed."

commands:
  auto_lacuna:
    label: "Find lacunae"
    effect: proposal-only
    operation: >
      Compare the current Orientation Map, inherited context, hard gates,
      objective state, and proof state. Surface the few missing, stale,
      contradictory, or decision-relevant coordinates most likely to change a
      rightful next choice.
    output: [candidate_lacuna, affected_coordinate, why_it_matters, source_refs, epistemic_status, confidence, next_question_or_hold, falsifier_or_close_condition]
    boundary: "It may not diagnose a person, invent an Agent, or convert absence into a claim."
  auto_cohere:
    label: "Auto-cohere"
    effect: proposal-only
    operation: >
      Recompile the current coordinate against its exact record, ancestor
      inheritance chain, lateral relationships, accepted preferences,
      objective dependencies, and current source freshness. Produce explicit
      patch proposals; never rewrite the holarchy in place.
    proposal_kinds: [answer_axis, correct_axis, mark_stale, add_lacuna, propose_primary_parent, propose_lateral_relation, propose_objective_dependency, propose_agent_candidate, split_coordinate, merge_coordinates, retire_projection, request_authority, request_proof]
    required_for_each_proposal: [proposal_id, target_coordinate, target_field_or_relation, before, after, rationale, source_refs, epistemic_status, confidence, affected_descendants, authority_required, expected_consequence, falsifier, accept_reject_or_defer_controls]
    topology_rule: >
      A primary-parent change is a structural proposal with descendant impact,
      conflict analysis, and an explicit owner/governance event. Lateral
      relevance does not create a second canonical parent.

proposal_feed:
  location: "The Yawn dialogue/event feed."
  actions: [accept, reject, correct, defer, inspect_sources]
  rule: >
    Every action creates or proposes an attributed event. Rejection and
    correction remain replayable evidence. Accepting a proposal does not prove
    its factual claim and does not authorize an external effect unless a
    separate authority contract explicitly does so.

coordinate_complete_minimum:
  meaning: >
    Enough context for a fresh authorized intelligence to orient without prompt
    archaeology while preserving unresolved uncertainty and links to deeper records.
  required: [coordinate_and_revision, principal_and_active_roles, relationship_and_Arena, governing_purpose_or_named_lacuna, current_state_and_open_lacunae, accepted_boundaries_and_authority, available_intelligence_capabilities_and_revocation, relevant_sources_and_epistemic_states, candidate_inquiry_hold_or_movement, proof_and_update_rule, parent_child_sibling_relationship_refs, stop_sleep_escalate_merge_split_retire_conditions]
  context_rule: >
    Compile a bounded working View with hashes and source refs. Summaries are
    cacheable projections; the source records remain inspectable and authoritative.

new_agent_spawn:
  default_state: candidate
  requires_before_activation: [proposed_identity_and_coordinate, parent_relationship, objective_or_explicit_discovery_mandate, Arena, capability_manifest, authority_and_effect_boundary, context_budget, communication_and_report_back_contract, proof_contract, stop_escalate_and_retire_conditions]
  report_back: >
    A child returns attributed observations, artifacts, consequences, lacunae,
    and proposals to the parent relationship. It cannot promote its own output
    to parent truth, inherit all parent authority, or recursively spawn beyond
    its grant.

illegal_casts:
  - "View -> ontology"
  - "generated answer -> accepted state"
  - "salience -> relevance"
  - "relevance -> meaning"
  - "confidence -> authority"
  - "recommendation -> choice"
  - "choice -> authorization"
  - "capability -> permission"
  - "movement -> proof"
  - "provider -> Agent identity"
  - "child grant -> parent authority"
  - "acceptance -> truth"
  - "resolution level -> human worth or intelligence rank"

proof:
  required_scenarios: [new_ambiguous_self_reflection_signal, new_relationship_coordinate_with_another_rightful_principal, new_delegated_software_work_Agent, existing_coordinate_receiving_contradictory_evidence, ordinary_object_or_topic_where_no_Agent_coordinate_should_be_created, proposed_reparenting_with_affected_descendants, disconnected_intelligence_provider, completed_move_with_consequence_but_insufficient_proof]
  success: >
    A fresh capable model can enter the resulting authorized coordinate, state
    who and where it is, name what is known and unknown, preserve authority,
    choose the next inquiry or explicit hold, and produce a replayable proposal
    without bespoke prompt reconstruction or silent canonical mutation.
  falsifier: >
    A simpler note/task interface performs equally or better on attribution,
    authority preservation, orientation quality, correction burden, proof
    closure, and retained user agency—or the grid induces false completeness,
    agent reification, compulsive filling, or topology churn.
